### **10 EasyDMA** 

EasyDMA is an easy-to-use direct memory access module that some peripherals implement to gain direct access to Data RAM. 

The EasyDMA is an AHB bus master similar to the CPU and it is connected to the AHB multilayer interconnect for direct access to the Data RAM. The EasyDMA is not able to access the Flash. 

A peripheral can implement multiple EasyDMA instances, for example to provide a dedicated channel for reading data from RAM into the peripheral at the same time as a second channel is dedicated for writing data to the RAM from the peripheral. This concept is illustrated in _Figure 6: EasyDMA example_ on page 28 



